# Logger interface (downstream)

External-state functionality. This is what fit, inspect, and lr_finder call. Backend constructors and vendor objects are not here.

A `Logger` is already built. Downstream never passes `log_dir`, URIs, or tags into these methods.

Named constants, no defaults.

```
LogStream     = fit | inspect
LogExistence  = create | require
```

W&B is not in this folder.

---

## What the caller is allowed to do

```
logger.setup(*, stream, existence)
logger.log_params(params)                          # Mapping[str, str]
logger.log_tags(tags)                              # Mapping[str, str]
logger.log_scalars(values, *, step)                # Mapping[str, float], step required
logger.log_image(tag, image, *, step)
logger.log_text(tag, text, *, step)
logger.log_table(tag, rows, *, step)
logger.close()
```

`log_scalar(tag, value, *, step)` is `log_scalars({tag: value}, step=step)`. Not a second algorithm.

`flatten_mapping` is a helper for the caller (nested config → `Mapping[str, str]`). It is not a logger method.

---

## `setup(*, stream, existence)`

Binds **this process** so `log_*` is legal. Both arguments required.

| Caller | Call |
|---|---|
| fit, rank 0 | `setup(stream=fit, existence=create)` |
| inspect | `setup(stream=inspect, existence=require)` |

DDP ranks other than 0 do not call `setup`. That is the caller, not the logger.

Illegal if already open. Backend algorithms: TensorBoard `tensorboard.mdc`, MLflow `mlflow.mdc`. Downstream does not branch on backend.

---

## `log_*`

Illegal if not open. Downstream does not re-check vendor state.

Fit: `log_params` once, `log_text` of the run config at `step=0`, `log_scalars` each epoch.

Inspect: `log_image` / `log_table` / `log_text` at `step=epoch`. Tag namespace `inspection/...` vs fit metrics is the caller’s.

No `log_artifact` / `log_model` on this interface.

Those two calls are MLflow artifact-store operations (and the input to Model Registry). They live on `MlflowLogger`. An engine that chose MLflow may call them because it already knows the backend. Fit, inspect, and lr_finder do not.

Inspect files that every backend must show in the UI go through `log_image` / `log_text` / `log_table`. Files that stay on disk under `inspection_runs/` are not logging.

---

## `close()`

Process-local. Idempotent. Does not finish, delete, or lock the vendor run. Other processes that `require` still can log.

Fit and inspect each `close` their own logger object.

---

## Not on this interface

- `__init__` — backend-specific (TB: `log_dir`, `run_name`; MLflow: URIs, `experiment_name`, `run_name`, tags).
- `run_id` / `tracking_uri` — MLflow internals. Engine does not read them from `Logger`.
- Manager objects.
- Locks, “one live fit / one live inspect” — engine.

---

## Translation (ABC)

```
setup(*, stream, existence)
log_params(params)
log_tags(tags)
log_scalars(values, *, step)
log_image(tag, image, *, step)
log_text(tag, text, *, step)
log_table(tag, rows, *, step)
close()
```
